  "description": "#5057 — the five remaining batch writers: `create_blocks_batch` and `move_blocks_batch`, which answer with a LIST OF ROWS, and `set_property_batch`, `set_todo_state_batch` and `add_tags_by_ids`, which answer with a bare COUNT. Both shapes are new to the command leg: a scalar return used to fall through `project_return`'s object branch and pin only the command name, so the count — the one thing a caller of those three can see — went unchecked. The rows pin ORDER as well as content, and the counts pin which rows a batch SKIPS, which is where a fold over single-block calls and a set-based batch diverge.",
